<title>JAPAN: Japan March aluminium imports up 14.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan March aluminium imports up 14.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined aluminium</p>
<p>imports totalled 223,313 tonnes in March, up 14.1 percent from</p>
<p>195,667 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry</p>
<p>statistics released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (on a customs-cleared basis,</p>
<p>in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     Mar 97    Feb 97	Mar 96</p>
<p> Total	    223,313   234,648     195,667</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Brazil	    20,161    18,038	29,788</p>
<p> Russia	    42,611    54,816	28,634</p>
<p> Australia	 31,551    41,594	36,824</p>
<p> U.S.		 8,732    11,593	13,017</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refined aluminium in the first three months of 1997 were 688,513 tonnes, up from 609,549 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
